{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ripening-lupine-turaco","creation_channel":"cli","description":"A ticket with a fresh, PASSing, correctly-pinned plan-review attestation cannot be claimed: the gate reports stale-pin-drift against a dependency that has not changed since the review was signed.\n\nObserved on 47e9-728e-ba93-485e (depends_on ae96-f114-5363-4d57). Gates on: verify.require_plan_review_for_claim, verify.enforce_plan_material_pins.\n\n## Evidence\n\n    $ rebar claim 47e9-728e-ba93-485e\n    Error: cannot start work on 47e9-728e-ba93-485e: reviewed related-ticket material is\n    stale (stale-pin-drift; targets: ae96-f114-5363-4d57).\n\n    $ rebar review-plan 47e9-728e-ba93-485e --status\n    signed_at = 1786115382183702000   verified_at_sha = 1afdbbd0be...\n\n    $ rebar show ae96-f114-5363-4d57  ->  updated_at = 1786100248773305001, status = closed\n\nThe attestation is signed ~15,133,000,000 ns (~4.2 hours) AFTER ae96's last recorded change. The\ndependency is closed and quiescent. The review nevertheless reports its pinned material as stale.\n\n## What was ruled out\n\n- NOT head staleness. That is a separate, distinct error on this same ticket\n  ('attestation is stale (unscoped; signed at 1afdbbd0be..., HEAD is 137d7ed633...)'), and it is\n  cleared by checking the worktree out at the attestation's verified_at_sha. Doing so surfaces the\n  pin-drift error underneath it, so the two are independent conditions, not one condition reported\n  twice.\n- NOT an ordering mistake. The sequence was: ae96 closed -> THEN review-plan 47e9 (PASS) -> claim.\n  The timestamps above confirm that ordering held.\n- NOT a stale verdict. Two consecutive review-plan runs on 47e9 both returned\n  {\"verdict\": \"PASS\"}; the block is at the claim gate, not the review.\n- NOT a dependency still in motion. ae96 is closed, and nothing wrote to it between the review and\n  the claim attempts.\n\n## Reproduction shape\n\n1. Ticket B depends_on ticket A.\n2. A is completed and CLOSED (the close writes status + signature events to A).\n3. review-plan B -> PASS, attestation signed at a time strictly later than A's updated_at.\n4. claim B -> refused with stale-pin-drift naming A.\n\nRepeating step 3 does not clear it; the second review produced the same verified_at_sha and the\nsame refusal.\n\n## Impact\n\n47e9-728e-ba93-485e is unclaimable through the normal path. Because the plan-review claim gate is\nenabled, there is no way to start work on it without --force, which AGENTS.md reserves for an\noperator's judgement call. Everything downstream of it in the same epic is consequently stalled:\n8efe-9ceb-7d89-4a33 and f0ff-028a-f5cb-4b66 depend on 47e9, and 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239 depends on\nboth of those.\n\nRelated but distinct: f680-4224-6553-48ca records a CLOSE-side gate deadlock. This one is on the\nCLAIM side and has a different trigger -- there no description edit is involved, and no\n[operator-attested] tag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A dependent whose attestation post-dates its dependency's last change is claimable without\n      --force, OR the additional condition that makes the pin stale is surfaced in the error\n      message so the operator can act on it","id":"3e0f-d90a-3b91-475c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"stale-pin-drift blocks a claim even when the attestation is newer than the pinned dependency's last change"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786116828118764001,"uuid":"45a55081-6811-421a-bb0c-9e2212ce13e7"}